<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Changamire</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Changamire was the title of the rulers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rozvi-empire">Rozvi Empire</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwean-plateau">Zimbabwe plateau</a>, taken from the founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changamire-dombo">Changamire Dombo</a>. The title had earlier been associated with a powerful figure within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa</a> state. The rise of the Changamire dynasty in the late seventeenth century supplanted Mutapa authority over much of the region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/changamire.jpg" alt="Changamire" width="320" height="247" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ypirétis · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Empire-rozvi.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
